# K0 / B009 — Run 2 replica annotation (blind).

C R241 OL GOV-013,GOV-012 | MUST NOT | Test the risks that matter and build test infrastructure only for a concrete testing need (no enterprise-sized harness for a small project, no generic test-data framework for a few simple objects, no snapshot library by default). | Backend tests | concrete testing need
C R242 OL TST-010 | MUST | Turn temporary behavioral probes (HTTP requests, shell/PowerShell scripts, ad-hoc test methods, manual database checks) into maintained tests (e.g. an ad-hoc curl becomes a WebApplicationFactory test); confirm an existing test really covers the behavior instead of adding a duplicate; review probes before keeping them. | Backend tests | equivalent existing coverage
C R243 OL DEP-009,ARC-023,DEP-001 | MUST | Register EF Core and persistence implementations in Infrastructure with the provider the project actually uses, not one that merely appears in an example. | EF Core registration | none stated
C R244 OL ARC-006,ARC-003 | MUST NOT | EF Core interceptors fit infrastructure-level cross-cutting behavior with a clear benefit (e.g. auditing); business behavior does not belong in them. | EF Core interceptors | none stated
C X29 EX RUN-002,ARC-022 | AVOID (listed common mistake) | Fire-and-forget EF Core asynchronous operations are listed as a mistake to avoid. | EF Core data access | none stated | RUN-002 forbids blocking async I/O and ARC-022 governs lifetimes; no oracle policy (and no K0 standard) forbids un-awaited database operations. | Starting EF Core queries without awaiting them is treated as a defect.

